Aim: To explore and practice basic Git and GitHub commands for version control.

Requirements:
- Git
- GitHub account
- Terminal / Git Bash
1. Configure Git
Set your username and email.
git config --global user.name "Vaishnavi"
git config --global user.email "vaishnavi@gmail.com"


Check configuration:
git config --list


Output:
user.name=Vaishnavi
user.email=vaishnavi@gmail.com


2. Create a local repository
mkdir DevOps
cd DevOps
git init


Output:
Initialized empty Git repository


3. Create a file
echo "Welcome to DevOps Lab" > file.txt


4. Check repository status
git status


Output:
Untracked files:
    file.txt


5. Add files to staging area
git add file.txt


6. Commit changes
git commit -m "First commit"


Output:
1 file changed


7. View commit history
git log --oneline


8. Create a branch
git branch feature


Switch to the branch:
git checkout feature


Or use:
git switch feature


9. Merge branches
Switch to the main branch:
git checkout main


Merge the feature branch:
git merge feature


10. Connect to GitHub
Create an empty repository on GitHub and copy its HTTPS URL.
git remote add origin https://github.com/username/DevOps.git


Rename the branch:
git branch -M main


Push the code:
git push -u origin main


11. Other important Git commands
Command	Purpose
git clone URL	Copy a remote repository
git pull	Download and integrate latest changes
git fetch	Download changes without merging
git push	Upload local commits
git diff	Show file differences
git status	Check repository status
git rm file.txt	Remove a tracked file
git stash	Temporarily save changes
git branch	Display branches
git reset	Move HEAD to another commit
